Let~$N$ be a simply-connected~$4$-manifold with boundary~$\partial N \cong S^3$ and let~$K \subset S^3$ be a knot.
Given a nondegenerate Hermitian form~$(H,\lambda)$ over~$\Z[t^{\pm 1}]$, the following assertions are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item
the Hermitian form~$(H,\lambda)$ presents~$M_{K,g}$ and satisfies~$\lambda(1)\cong Q_N \oplus (0)^{\oplus 2g}$;
\item the set~$\operatorname{Surf(g)}^0_\lambda(N,K)$ is nonempty and there is a bijection
$$\operatorname{Surf(g)}^0_\lambda(N,K) \approx \Iso(\partial \lambda,\unaryminus\Bl_{M_{K,g}})/(\Aut(\lambda)\times \operatorname{Homeo}^+(\Sigma_{g,1},\partial)).$$
\end{enumerate}

